u/11538601?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheClave","html_url":"https://github.com/TheClave","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheClave/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheClave/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheClave/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheClave/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheClave/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheClave/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheClave/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheClave/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheClave/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-15T21:44:07Z","updated_at":"2026-03-15T21:44:07Z","body":"> > Yes, you are right, disabling the Screen Space Roughness Limiter indeed removes the artifacts, but it also removes all specular reflections, which is mostly undesirable.\n> \n> Setting roughness to 0 is actually what removes specular highlights, if you set it to a low nonzero amount you should see them again.\n\nYes, by tweaking the values I can achieve desirable results :) I will close this issue then. Thank you again for your support!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4063957893/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]